course: dictionary
lesson: 4946
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Imprint is one of them. Look at the words around it: if the sentence talks about a mark pressed into mud or a coin, it means a mark; if it talks about memory or feelings, it means a lasting effect.
explain: «Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching, usually their mother; this is called imprinting, and ducklings have imprinted on people, dogs and even boots.» Here imprinting means a young animal learns to follow the first thing it sees. The clues are «follow» and «the first moving thing they see».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the swap still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An imprint is a mark or shape pressed into a surface, like a footprint in mud.
fact: An imprint can also be a lasting effect, such as an experience that leaves its imprint on someone.
fact: To imprint something on your mind is to fix it firmly in your memory.
fact: In biology, imprinting means a young animal learns to follow the first thing it sees, usually its mother.
fact: A publisher's imprint is the brand name it puts on a book.
exercise: Fossils are often imprints of leaves in rock. What is an imprint here? | A tiny crack in a window | A green plant that grows in water | A loud noise made by rock | *A mark or shape pressed into a surface
exercise: «Ducklings have imprinted on people, dogs and even boots.» What does imprinted mean here? | Fell into the water | *Learned to follow, having seen them first | Were drawn in a picture | Got wet and cold
exercise: To imprint a design on a coin is to do what? | *Press the design onto it | Melt the coin | Hide the coin | Count the coins
test: What does imprint mean when you say you imprint a name on your mind? | To shout it loudly | To write it on a list | To rub it out | *To fix it firmly in your memory
test: A publisher's imprint is what? | A picture on the front cover | *A brand name put on a book | A page number | A kind of paper
exam: Which sentence uses imprint to mean a mark pressed into a surface? | *A footprint left in the mud | A story that left an imprint on her heart | A book with a publisher's imprint | A friend who imprinted on her memory
